  "answer": "This crash has been reported before. It is a WPF 'Cyclic reference found while evaluating the Style property' exception, and it is thrown when Windows broadcasts a system theme change. That broadcast can happen at boot, at login, on wake from sleep, or on a light/dark or accent change. The stack trace points to PowerToys Run. The trace in #47501 matches yours, including the ListView with 15 items. #45730 has the same ListView trace and was closed as a duplicate of #36451, which is the main tracking issue. I found no fix or confirmed workaround in these tickets. You can add your 0.100.2.0 report, your Windows 11 build and the fact that it runs in a Parallels VM to #36451. A maintainer also asked in #47501 whether the crash coincided with a theme or accent change, an automatic light/dark switch, or resuming from sleep. Telling them would help. As a mitigation, you can turn off PowerToys Run in Settings, or turn off automatic theme switching. I haven't confirmed that either one stops the crash, because the tickets don't say."
 },
